<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly residues down, distillates down.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly residues down, distillates down.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks fell by 984,000 barrels in the week ended August 28 to 9.07 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks fell by 200,000 barrels to 7.423 million barrels.</p>
<p>Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks were down by 168,000 barrels to 4.711 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha. -- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
